# tally 2.3.1 R3: a `with known` pin and an `as known` clause on one line are two pins of the cut, so
# LOAD-OVERLAP. Before: 10.00 PLN, the cut 2026-03-01.
=== lawpin_q7.tally
model lawpin
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input w: date
input rate: money PLN

def cost: money PLN at reader
  rule one = rate

ask q7: cost with known 2026-03-01 law 2026-03-01 as known 2026-05-01


version v
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..2026-06-30
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 10.00 PLN "s"

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-07-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 20.00 PLN "s"

version v3
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = 2026-02-01 "s"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-OVERLAP pins known 2026-03-01 and as known 2026-05-01 of the cut overlap at no keys (lawpin_q7.tally:15)
